{1 = 1-5}
1.	Say to @wDN{Utu} my lord, the exalted judge of heaven and earth, who cares for the Land, who renders verdicts; just god, who loves to keep man alive, who heeds entreaty, who extends mercy, who knows …… compassion, who loves justice, who selects honesty, ……: 

{6 = 6-11}
6.	Repeat to the bearded one, the son of @wDN{Ningal}, …… a lapis-lazuli beard, @varh[t3205.v1]{who opens the bolts of heaven and earth } @vart[t3205.v2,t3205.v1]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} who opens the bolts }, who creates brightness in darkness; foremost lord who alone is resplendent, whose greatness is unequalled; warrior, son given birth by @wDN{Ningal}, who guards and gathers together the divine powers; just god, prince who determines all the fates, my lord, father of the black-headed: this is what @wRN{@wDN{Sîn}-iddinam}, king of @wSN{Larsam}, your servant, says: 

{12 = 12-20}
12.	Distress has been caused in your city @wSN{Larsam}, which you have chosen in your heart. 
13.	The broad squares where days have been passed in merriment @varh[t3205.v3]{have been reduced to } @vart[t3205.v4,t3205.v3]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} are left (?) in } silence. 
14.	Your commendable troops who were assembled have been annihilated (?) like reeds from a reed fence splitting apart. 
15.	Your young men have been harvested like barley at the due time; they have been picked and have been plucked like ripened fruit (?). 
16.	The people have been smashed like terracotta figurines; they (?) have perished all together. 
17.	An evil storm took away the little ones from the laps (?) of their mothers. 
18.	The people ……; their appearance has been (?) changed. 
19.	Overwhelming troops have been set loose, …… the Land …… like flour. 
20.	O youthful @wDN{Utu}, like an enemy you stand aside from your city @wSN{Larsam}. 

